{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>I call to witness against you this day the heavens and the earth.</b> For they endure forever, and when evil befalls you they will be witnesses that I warned you about all this. Another matter — <b>I call to witness against you this day the heavens etc.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel: Look at the heavens that I created to serve you — perhaps they changed their nature? Perhaps the orb of the sun did not rise from the east and illuminate the whole world, as it says (Ecclesiastes 1): ״וְזָרַח הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ וּבָא הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ״? Look at the earth that I created to serve you — perhaps it changed its nature? Perhaps you seeded it and it did not sprout, or perhaps you seeded wheat and it yielded barley? Now these, which were made for neither reward nor loss — if they succeed they receive no reward, and if they sin they receive no punishment — did not change their nature; you, who if you succeed receive reward and if you sin receive punishment — how much more so! (Sifrei Deuteronomy 32)." "<b>And you shall choose life.</b> I am directing you to choose the portion of life — like a person who says to his son: Choose a fine portion in my inheritance, and he stands him over the fine portion and says to him: This one, take for yourself. And of this it says (Psalms 16): ״HaShem is my allotted portion and my cup; You support my lot״ — You placed my hand upon the good lot, to say: This one, take for yourself."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:01.336042922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}